:answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186460993}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "cb3a08e1-046c-5655-8701-2c4bac14eb96" :question/math-academy-id "q-80234" :question/problem "To which of the following sets does the number $-5$ belong?\n\nSelect all that apply." :question/worked-solution "![](images/67/67ef97be4b21a74feaae15f3ff30d5077fc1316874df8de79155316a621e4487.png)\n\nRecall the following:\n\n- $N$ represents the set of **natural numbers**.\n\n- $Z$ represents the set of **integers**.\n\n- $Q$ represents the set of **rational numbers**.\n\n- $R$ represents the set of **real numbers**.\n\n- $C$ represents the set of **complex numbers**\n\nWith that in mind, we note the following:\n\n- The number $-5$ is negative, so it does *not* belong to $N,$ and we can write\n\n$$\n-5\\notin N.\n$$\n\n- However, $-5$ is an integer, so it does belong to $Z,$ and we can write\n\n$$\n-5\\in Z.\n$$\n\n- Every integer is a rational, real, and complex number. Consequently, $-5$ belongs to $Q,R,$ and $C,$ and we can write\n\n$$\n-5\\in Q,\\,-5\\in R,\\,-5\\in C.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"$Z,Q,R,$ and $C.$\""} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186055500 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "d676c3f1-3e6a-54fd-a188-1f7fc71793be" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$N$ and $Z$ only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186054238} {:answer/id #uuid "4a13ac46-b378-57d3-a22c-3f4d04a9175c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$Z$ only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186054239} {:answer/id #uuid "4ad40235-d04d-5b92-9a1e-821434e1b825" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$N, Z, Q, R$, and $C$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186054240} {:answer/id #uuid "798b1f3c-33bd-5d07-b749-ac0418bd8a2b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$N$ only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186054241} {:answer/id #uuid "7a4f6a7d-4b25-5a31-9fe8-a201cb04f4bc