 {:db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186466688}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "fcd97869-92b9-51fc-a566-7b09c1bf865d" :question/math-academy-id "q-181522" :question/problem "To which of the following sets does the number $\\sqrt{-4}$ belong?\n\nSelect all that apply." :question/worked-solution "![](images/67/67ef97be4b21a74feaae15f3ff30d5077fc1316874df8de79155316a621e4487.png)\n\nRecall the following:\n\n- $N$ represents the set of **natural numbers**.\n\n- $Z$ represents the set of **integers**.\n\n- $Q$ represents the set of **rational numbers**.\n\n- $R$ represents the set of **real numbers**.\n\n- $C$ represents the set of **complex numbers**\n\nWith that in mind, we note the following:\n\n- First, we note that $\\sqrt{-4}=2\\text{i}$ is a complex number. Therefore, we can write\n\n$$\n\\sqrt{-4}\\in C.\n$$\n\n- Since the imaginary part of $\\sqrt{-4}$ is nonzero, it does *not* belong to $N,Z,Q,$ or $R.$ We can write\n\n$$\n\\sqrt{-4}\\notin N,\\,\\sqrt{-4}\\notin Z,\\,\\sqrt{-4}\\notin Q,\\,\\sqrt{-4}\\notin R.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"$C$ only.\""} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186348364 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "8fb1cc51-1db2-57b9-baf6-75de2e4cdec8" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186469148} {:answer/id #uuid "dbccee3c-0547-5c53-8dfb-7fa8ba086442" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186469149}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "dbccee3c-0547-5c53-8dfb-7fa8ba086442" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186469149} :answer-field/id #uuid "1f5e3c87-547e-5a51-a277-73a08a1f920c" :answer-field/key "Complex numbers ($C$)" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186470186} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "f6b1ec93-9b14-50ab-8952-12494ec08ede"