"29c30ac2-34fa-5d4b-81fc-1b6392637753" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186622946} :answer-field/id #uuid "fceb4996-bc39-5928-8d23-8fbc0d681387" :answer-field/key "Real numbers ($R$)" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186623013}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "19e48cbb-c9c8-54e6-ae30-e26b9d815aeb" :question/problem "To which of the following sets does the number $\\frac{56}{7}$ belong?\n\nSelect all that apply." :question/worked-solution "![](images/67/67ef97be4b21a74feaae15f3ff30d5077fc1316874df8de79155316a621e4487.png)\n\nRecall the following:\n\n- $N$ represents the set of **natural numbers**.\n\n- $Z$ represents the set of **integers**.\n\n- $Q$ represents the set of **rational numbers**.\n\n- $R$ represents the set of **real numbers**.\n\n- $C$ represents the set of **complex numbers**.\n\nWith that in mind, we note the following:\n\n- The number $\\frac{56}{7}=8$ is a positive whole number, so it belongs to $N.$ We can write\n\n$$\n\\frac{56}{7}\\in N\n$$\n\n- Every natural number is an integer, rational, real, and complex number. Consequently, we can write\n\n$$\n\\begin{gathered}\\frac{56}{7}\\in Z\\qquad \\frac{56}{7}\\in Q \\\\ \\frac{56}{7}\\in R\\qquad \\frac{56}{7}\\in C\\end{gathered}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is $N, Z, Q, R, C$."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186622952 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "4b91e5e6-26e7-5c11-a55a-779599b7a0f5" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186622956} {:answer/id #uuid "a8065df6-811c-5529-b9e5-ff5854f5fa0f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186622984}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "a8065df6-811c-5529-b9e5-ff5854f5fa0f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186622984} :answer-field