number $-6.20$ belong?\n\nSelect all that apply." :question/worked-solution "![](images/67/67ef97be4b21a74feaae15f3ff30d5077fc1316874df8de79155316a621e4487.png)\n\nRecall the following:\n\n- $N$ represents the set of **natural numbers**.\n\n- $Z$ represents the set of **integers**.\n\n- $Q$ represents the set of **rational numbers**.\n\n- $R$ represents the set of **real numbers**.\n\n- $C$ represents the set of **complex numbers**.\n\nWith that in mind, we note the following:\n\n- The number $-6.20$ is not an integer, so it does *not* belong to $Z$ nor to $N.$ We can write\n\n$$\n-6.20\\notin N\\qquad -6.20\\notin Z\n$$\n\n- However, it can be written as the ratio of two integers:\n\n$$\n-6.20=-\\frac{620}{100}\n$$\n\nConsequently, $-6.20$ is a rational number, and we can write\n\n$$\n-6.20\\in Q\n$$\n\n- Every rational is a real and complex number. Consequently, $-6.20$ belongs to both $R$ and $C,$ and we can write\n\n$$\n-6.20\\in R\\qquad -6.20\\in C\n$$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is $Q, R, C$ only."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186622991 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "98be678a-3843-59d0-9590-9e830cc1e87b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186622980} {:answer/id #uuid "fba6bf22-633d-5d1b-b63d-c0453437493f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186623011}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "98be678a-3843-59d0-9590-9e830cc1e87b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186622980} :answer-field/id #uuid "280f5a7c-157e-545c-9f8e-194b0ea69a38" :answer-field/key "Complex numbers ($C$)" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186622945} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "33f6ab46-5fba-5b8e-a511-cde786568910" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186622951} {:answer/id #uuid "d48e6925-83ac-56a0