{:db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186673706} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "ae63ac59-d057-5432-860e-d0e4844a340c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186673711} {:answer/id #uuid "dd0f265d-bfa5-50dc-a4a6-2e74cd7fa586" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186673719}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "ae63ac59-d057-5432-860e-d0e4844a340c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186673711} :answer-field/id #uuid "ef087a7a-dda5-5c8e-9e5f-dec5cb3d178c" :answer-field/key "Natural numbers ($N$)" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186673723}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "db5a74cd-1494-5d20-90cc-b56ee7af9d16" :question/problem "To which of the following sets does the number $\\sqrt{58}$ belong?\n\nSelect all that apply." :question/worked-solution "![](images/67/67ef97be4b21a74feaae15f3ff30d5077fc1316874df8de79155316a621e4487.png)\n\nRecall the following:\n\n- $N$ represents the set of **natural numbers**.\n\n- $Z$ represents the set of **integers**.\n\n- $Q$ represents the set of **rational numbers**.\n\n- $R$ represents the set of **real numbers**.\n\n- $C$ represents the set of **complex numbers**.\n\nWith that in mind, we note the following:\n\n- The number $\\sqrt{58}$ is not an integer, so it does *not* belong to $Z$ nor to $N.$ We can write\n\n$$\n\\sqrt{58}\\notin N\\qquad \\sqrt{58}\\notin Z\n$$\n\n- Also, $\\sqrt{58}$ is irrational because $58$ is positive and not a perfect square. It cannot be written as the ratio of two integers, so it does *not* belong to $Q$ either:\n\n$$\n\\sqrt{58}\\notin Q\n$$\n\n- Every irrational number is both a real number and a complex number. Consequently, $\\sqrt{58}$ belongs to both $R$ and $C,$ and we can write\n\n$$\n\\sqrt{58}\\in R\\qquad \\sqrt{58}\\in C\n$$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is $R, C$ only."}] :knowledge-point/title "Identifying Special Sets Containing a Given Element"}]}
